# NFILT (enter a filter: wavelength / flux pairs, 0 ends), SFILT (write it as <name>.filt), RFILT (read it back),
# MULTISPEC (the multi-color stack) on a COPY of the manual's Cassegrain in $TMP (cmdref: Source & Wavelength).
# The .filt format is the reader's and the field files': a header line '<name> <nWavelen>', one line of
# wavelengths, one line of fluxes per star type (the cmdref example reads 10 wavelengths and 2 star types).
# Fixed 2026-10-18 (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (o), ruled): the WRITER was wrong -- a stray 'nStarType=0' wrote no
# flux rows (and zeroed the session's count), so RFILT read 0 star types and MULTISPEC refused every one; its
# list-directed header wrote the 256-wide name.  And the READER's list-directed header read stopped at the first
# '/' (a path) before the count.  Now SFILT -> RFILT -> MULTISPEC round-trips the NFILT filter (both wavelengths
# at their fluxes), a path name round-trips, and a field-format file whose header name holds a '/' reads 3
# wavelengths / 2 star types and feeds star type 2.  Before any filter is loaded MULTISPEC says so.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
cd $TMP
old $DECK
none
multispec
nfilt
myfilt
6.0e-7
1.0
6.5e-7
0.5
0
sfilt
myfilt
! cat $TMP/myfilt.filt
rfilt
myfilt
multispec
5
1
64
2e-6
sfilt
$TMP/sub_dir_name
rfilt
$TMP/sub_dir_name
! printf 'field/filt 3\n5.0e-7 6.0e-7 7.0e-7\n1.0 1.0 1.0\n0.5 1.0 0.5\n' > $TMP/field.filt
rfilt
field
multispec
5
2
64
2e-6
! ls $TMP
# EXPECT: Load filter data first\.
# EXPECT: Filter includes information for\s+2 wavelengths and\s+1 star types\.
# EXPECT: Filter file created\.
# EXPECT: ^myfilt\.filt 2\s*$
# EXPECT: ^\s+1\.0+\s+0\.50*\s*$
# EXPECT: MACOS> rfilt\s+Enter filter file name: myfilt\s+Filter includes information for\s+2 wavelengths and\s+1 star types\.
# EXPECT: Enter StarType \(1-1\): \[1\]: 1[\s\S]*?Wavelength= 6\.0000000D-07;  Source Flux= 1\.0000000D\+00[\s\S]*?Sum of intensity= 9\.2031079D\+08[\s\S]*?Wavelength= 6\.5000000D-07;  Source Flux= 5\.0000000D-01[\s\S]*?Sum of intensity= 3\.9208507D\+08
# EXPECT: Enter filter file name: \S+/sub_dir_name\s+Filter includes information for\s+2 wavelengths and\s+1 star types\.
# EXPECT: Enter filter file name: field\s+Filter includes information for\s+3 wavelengths and\s+2 star types\.
# EXPECT: Enter StarType \(1-2\): \[1\]: 2[\s\S]*?Wavelength= 5\.0000000D-07;  Source Flux= 5\.0000000D-01[\s\S]*?Wavelength= 6\.0000000D-07;  Source Flux= 1\.0000000D\+00[\s\S]*?Wavelength= 7\.0000000D-07;  Source Flux= 5\.0000000D-01
# EXPECT: myfilt\.filt
# EXPECT-NOT: Invalid star type
# EXPECT-NOT: not in expected format
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
